    "note": "Text read is the 6th Substitute (02-13-24), listed as 'Introduced'; the House passed 2-15-2024 (42-26) but later amendments are not in the text read. Credit applies to devices bought Jan 1, 2024 to Jan 1, 2027. Tax credit is the gun-safety measure itself, so not counted as a separate taxes subject."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new Utah Code 59-10-1048): (2) An eligible claimant may claim a nonrefundable tax credit under this section in an amount equal to the lesser of: (a) the purchase price of the firearm safety device; or (b) $50.\nSection 1 (new Utah Code 59-10-1048): (1)(c)(i) \"Firearm safety device\" means equipment designed to prevent the unauthorized access to, or operation or discharge of, a firearm.\nSection 1 (new Utah Code 59-10-1048): (4) An eligible claimant may not: (a) claim more than one tax credit under this section;\nSection 2 (Utah Code 63I-1-259): (9) Section 59-10-1048 is repealed July 1, 2027."
}